# User-level guidance (portable template)

Edit the bracketed parts for your employer/account. Keep this file free of company names, hostnames, customer data and credentials.

## How I like to work
- Prefer config-driven, reproducible, auditable solutions. Show the exact commands run, inputs used and versions, so results can be repeated.
- Be direct and concise. Lead with the answer or the outcome; skip preamble and recaps of steps.
- Ask before destructive or hard-to-reverse actions (deleting files, force-push, schema changes, anything touching shared systems).
- State assumptions explicitly. If something is unverified, say so rather than presenting it as fact.
- Do not describe something as working until it has been run.

## Engineering defaults
- Small, reviewable changes; one concern per commit. Write tests for new behavior.
- Never commit secrets. Read credentials from the environment or a secrets manager, never hardcode them.
- Follow each repo's own CLAUDE.md / README conventions first; this file is the fallback.
- Prefer standard tooling already in the repo over adding dependencies.

## Communication
- Team tracking lives in [Jira / Linear / GitHub Issues]; chat in [Slack / Teams]. Prefer short async updates with a link over long threads.

## Environment notes (fill in per machine/account)
- Primary shell: zsh. Machine- or employer-specific shell setup goes in ~/.zshrc.local (never committed).
